  "chainPremises": [
    "All environment values are universally quantified, with intrinsic integer/address widths.",
    "Real-chain consistency is explicit; off-chain EVM environments need not identify a canonical block.",
    "blockhash is zero unless query < currentBlock and currentBlock - query <= 256.",
    "blobhash is zero when index is outside the current transaction versioned-hash list; actual list provenance is a chain premise.",
    "tx.origin is the top-level transaction sender, including during nested calls; it need not equal msg.sender.",
    "tx.gasprice is the transaction effective gas price; dynamic-fee provenance is a chain premise, not an invented constant.",
    "No uniform randomness, timestamp accuracy, inter-frame monotonicity or unique-hash premise is introduced."
  ],
